WEBVTT

00:08.500 --> 00:11.030
<i>The insurgent leader and three magical girls</i>

00:11.030 --> 00:13.520
<i>are confirmed at the Nakano warehouse.</i>

00:13.520 --> 00:19.030
<i>Currently, forces occupying the Sotokanda 
area are assumed to be infantry only.</i>

00:19.700 --> 00:24.020
<i>Immobilize the insurgent forces 
and "protect" the subjects.</i>

00:24.020 --> 00:26.760
<i>All units, commence operations!</i>

00:31.330 --> 00:32.390
What?

00:32.390 --> 00:33.380
What's up?

00:34.420 --> 00:36.380
Huh? Rinna-chan?

00:38.190 --> 00:39.380
We're under attack!

00:39.380 --> 00:40.880
On your feet, soldiers!

00:41.300 --> 00:43.430
Damn it! It's still the middle of the night!

00:43.430 --> 00:45.520
Curse you SSC cowards!

00:45.520 --> 00:48.200
All troops, prepare for battle!

02:30.800 --> 02:32.760
Damn it! They're attacking now?!

02:33.620 --> 02:35.710
Come in, Otaku Hero!

02:35.710 --> 02:36.640
No good.

02:36.640 --> 02:39.440
Is that son of a bitch dead?

02:40.800 --> 02:43.260
Ah, damn it! You, over there!

02:43.260 --> 02:45.180
<i>Enemy on your seven!</i>

02:50.370 --> 02:51.730
You saved me, Nick!

02:51.730 --> 02:53.120
<i>Stay alert, you idiot!</i>

02:53.120 --> 02:55.240
Hey, you can see things from there, right?

02:55.240 --> 02:56.810
Help us fight!

02:56.810 --> 02:58.730
<i>I-I'm totally useless at fighting.</i>

02:58.730 --> 03:01.410
Otaku Hero and the girls aren't here!

03:01.410 --> 03:02.820
<i>Take command from there!</i>

03:06.010 --> 03:07.470
I'll do what I can.

03:07.470 --> 03:08.540
Stay on your toes!

03:08.540 --> 03:09.760
Don't let us down!

03:10.280 --> 03:13.220
Huge force advancing 
from the south side of Mansei Bridge.

03:13.220 --> 03:15.990
Nearby troops, concentrate your fire there!

03:15.990 --> 03:18.800
<i>Frontline units, pick someone to handle
communications and supplies!</i>

03:18.800 --> 03:22.050
<i>Troops in back, bring out all 
the lumber and Molotovs you can!</i>

03:22.050 --> 03:23.430
Otaku
<b>Canned Oden</b>

03:41.710 --> 03:43.290
<i>Why now?</i>

03:43.290 --> 03:45.590
<i>Even if they found out Otaku Hero was gone,</i>

03:45.590 --> 03:48.580
<i>how were they ready to attack so soon?</i>

03:49.100 --> 03:50.790
<i>It's always like this.</i>

03:50.790 --> 03:53.620
<i>We're always playing catch-up in battle.</i>

03:54.650 --> 03:59.380
<i>And we still don't know 
a damn thing about the enemy.</i>

04:36.790 --> 04:39.090
Come now, open your eyes.

04:39.090 --> 04:41.180
Your name is Slayer.

05:22.990 --> 05:24.500
Slayer...

05:24.500 --> 05:26.360
You don't mind, do you?

05:26.360 --> 05:28.510
Fine, but only when we're alone.

05:41.320 --> 05:42.520
Gobo.

05:45.880 --> 05:46.780
Okay.

05:48.870 --> 05:51.050
Pee-yew! What is this place?

05:51.050 --> 05:51.910
Drainage tunnel.

05:51.910 --> 05:53.510
A covered-up river.

05:53.510 --> 05:55.000
Gobo-bo gobo.

05:53.740 --> 05:55.000
"No problem for me."

05:55.000 --> 05:58.410
I've never seen your 
mask come in handy before.

06:00.920 --> 06:03.510
I'm worried my nose will 
get used to the smell.

06:03.510 --> 06:05.400
Gobo, gobo gobo gobo!

06:05.400 --> 06:07.050
Quit bragging, you showoff.

06:07.890 --> 06:10.800
I need to take a bath! Geez.

06:11.950 --> 06:16.050
One, two! One, two!

06:16.050 --> 06:19.320
If I l-leave them outside, 
they'll f-freeze to d-death.

06:19.320 --> 06:23.940
It's n-not like 
I'm trying something d-dirty.

06:24.520 --> 06:26.320
<i>And now the news.</i>

06:26.320 --> 06:29.340
<i>Following the nation-wide protection 
measures initiated in June,</i>

06:29.340 --> 06:31.230
<i>the SSC announced they 
are strengthening efforts</i>

06:31.230 --> 06:33.450
<i>to track down otaku 
who have slipped through their net</i>

06:33.450 --> 06:40.850
<i>and have asked for the public's 
understanding as they expand their program.</i>

06:41.240 --> 06:44.910
<i>Half a year since the start 
of otaku protection efforts,</i>

06:41.850 --> 06:47.290
<i>I got g-girls for C-Christmas. 
Three of them!</i>

06:44.920 --> 06:49.290
<i>public response to the measures 
is increasingly positive.</i>

06:50.520 --> 06:52.660
Merry Christmas!

06:50.520 --> 06:52.660
Gobo gobo!

06:52.660 --> 06:54.270
Help yourself to cake!

06:52.660 --> 06:54.270
Gobo-bo gobo!

06:54.270 --> 06:56.600
Thank you very much!

06:56.600 --> 06:57.970
What?

06:57.970 --> 06:58.920
Huh?

07:01.280 --> 07:02.260
Huh?!

07:02.730 --> 07:04.650
Oh, yum.

07:06.790 --> 07:09.030
It's happening!

07:12.960 --> 07:15.080
Wh-What's going on?!

07:16.580 --> 07:18.760
Oh, no! Ouch!

07:18.760 --> 07:20.380
Are you the one who found us?

07:21.050 --> 07:22.600
Uh...

07:22.600 --> 07:24.960
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

07:24.960 --> 07:28.080
Did you reincarnate us as magical girls?

07:28.080 --> 07:32.790
Yes, it was me. I'm sorry! 
Please don't report me!

07:33.110 --> 07:35.360
Eh? Magical girls?

07:36.280 --> 07:37.480
Gobo gobogo-bo.

07:37.480 --> 07:40.010
"We are magical girls."

07:40.010 --> 07:42.270
You mean everything to us.

07:43.240 --> 07:46.310
Everything? Wh-What are you—

07:46.310 --> 07:47.710
They're like babies.

07:47.710 --> 07:48.280
Huh?

07:48.280 --> 07:51.520
Anarchy. Blue. Pink.

07:52.270 --> 07:55.210
Since you're the first person 
they saw after waking up,

07:55.210 --> 07:58.060
they recognize you as their 
parental figure or master.

08:00.540 --> 08:04.230
I-Is that what they meant, Kyotaro?

08:04.230 --> 08:05.040
Yeah.

08:05.040 --> 08:08.540
F-For now, I guess they need some clothes.

08:09.790 --> 08:10.550
Huh?

08:10.550 --> 08:13.130
You have no memory?

08:13.130 --> 08:13.970
Yeah.

08:16.100 --> 08:17.880
Delicious!

08:17.880 --> 08:19.280
Otaku
<b>Canned Oden</b>

08:19.280 --> 08:22.140
This must be a Kanto flavor. Too stronk!

08:24.650 --> 08:25.910
Are you dumb?

08:25.910 --> 08:27.650
Just take off your mask.

08:28.900 --> 08:32.230
W-Wait a sec. You mean you 
really forgot everything?

08:32.230 --> 08:32.980
Yeah.

08:32.980 --> 08:34.320
They're total airheads.

08:35.280 --> 08:37.280
But maybe we didn't forget.

08:37.280 --> 08:39.950
I think we were probably just born.

08:39.950 --> 08:41.560
Oh. Huh...

08:41.560 --> 08:44.400
So, you know, why don't you start telling us

08:44.400 --> 08:47.200
all about this world. And about you.

08:48.840 --> 08:53.380
Half a year ago, 
this country suddenly went crazy.

08:54.640 --> 08:59.900
An organization called SSC appeared, 
and they started "protecting" otaku like me.

09:01.840 --> 09:05.100
No, it wasn't protection. It was oppression.

09:05.470 --> 09:09.360
They stole all the merch 
and rounded up the otaku one by one.

09:11.360 --> 09:13.520
<b>Otaku Protection Rates</b>

09:13.520 --> 09:16.640
Akihabara was bombed to bits and closed off.

09:16.030 --> 09:17.910
<b>Pedestrian Zone in Effect</b>

09:17.910 --> 09:20.210
They stored the stolen goods in Nakano.

09:18.910 --> 09:20.660
General Fan

09:20.860 --> 09:23.950
And they turned Big Sight in Ariake 
into an internment camp.

09:26.000 --> 09:30.050
Now there's no place left 
for otaku to live in peace.

09:30.050 --> 09:30.900
Huh.

09:30.900 --> 09:32.650
What a tragedy!

09:32.650 --> 09:34.920
If they find this place, 
they won't let me off easy.

09:34.920 --> 09:38.520
But I'm not willing to roll over yet.

09:39.020 --> 09:40.680
I'm really sorry, but once you eat that

09:41.250 --> 09:42.680
would you please leave?

09:44.680 --> 09:46.080
Otaku
<b>Canned Oden</b>

09:44.680 --> 09:46.080
<b>Beef Tendon
Daikon</b>

10:02.520 --> 10:03.960
How're things on your side?

10:03.960 --> 10:05.080
It's really tough.

10:05.480 --> 10:08.000
They're hunting otaku all over Japan.

10:06.200 --> 10:06.830
<b>Yakisoba</b>

10:08.000 --> 10:09.480
Some are so afraid of someone ratting them out,

10:09.480 --> 10:12.010
they went deep in the mountains 
to live off the land.

10:12.010 --> 10:13.340
To live off the land?

10:13.340 --> 10:15.590
They take soil from the fields they plowed

10:15.590 --> 10:16.960
and mold figurines from it.

10:16.960 --> 10:18.720
That sounds awful.

10:19.090 --> 10:22.840
They can get supplies from friends posing 
as normies, but who knows for how long.

10:22.840 --> 10:25.000
This can't go on forever.

10:25.000 --> 10:26.920
We have to let otaku across Japan know

10:26.920 --> 10:29.350
that our flame still burns bright.

10:29.720 --> 10:31.040
Yeah, you're right.

10:31.640 --> 10:32.730
By the way...

10:34.730 --> 10:35.520
Here.

10:35.980 --> 10:36.470
Huh?

10:36.470 --> 10:37.010
Hey!

10:37.010 --> 10:39.110
What the hell is up with these girls?

10:39.280 --> 10:43.200
That's Anarchy-chan, 
Blue-chan, and Pink-chan.

10:43.200 --> 10:46.340
You built a harem 
to chill in all by yourself?!

10:46.340 --> 10:47.920
I'll kick your frickin' ass!

10:47.920 --> 10:49.200
Yes, sir!

10:50.650 --> 10:52.200
Gobobo bo bo.

10:52.200 --> 10:54.080
Go-bo-bo.

10:54.080 --> 10:57.280
Go bo-bo bo-bo, go gogo bobo.

10:57.280 --> 11:01.960
Gobo bobo bo-bo gobo...

10:59.340 --> 11:01.960
"Akihabara Maid Café Map"?

11:01.960 --> 11:05.470
Must be her thing. She's been staring 
at that page forever.

11:05.810 --> 11:07.460
You want to go to a maid café?

11:07.840 --> 11:09.820
Do you actually want to 
become a maid or something?

11:09.820 --> 11:10.970
Gobo!

11:10.970 --> 11:12.590
Gobo! Gobobo! Gobo!

11:12.590 --> 11:13.760
"Yeah," she says.

11:13.760 --> 11:15.800
You sure do love attention, don't you?

11:15.800 --> 11:18.200
Gobo! Gobo gobo!

11:18.200 --> 11:19.320
My bad.

11:18.530 --> 11:20.260
What are you listening to, Blue-chan?

11:23.150 --> 11:24.070
This!

11:24.070 --> 11:26.380
Oh, New Order!

11:26.380 --> 11:27.740
I love this one!

11:27.740 --> 11:29.670
Finally, someone gets it!

11:29.670 --> 11:31.660
Aren't their sequencers insane?

11:31.660 --> 11:32.760
Yeah, yeah!

11:32.760 --> 11:35.350
This track was breakthrough 
in digital music!

11:35.350 --> 11:36.400
The member of their earlier band...

11:36.400 --> 11:38.080
Gobo, gobo!

11:38.080 --> 11:41.190
Hmm? An authentic English-style maid café?

11:41.190 --> 11:43.530
Oh, nice! You would 
totally fit in, Pink-chan!

11:43.530 --> 11:45.520
Gobo? Gobo gobo!

11:50.790 --> 11:54.270
Hey, what kind of a place is Akihabara?

11:54.270 --> 11:56.360
I don't know...

11:59.720 --> 12:00.650
Take that!

12:01.920 --> 12:02.950
Yeah!

12:13.750 --> 12:18.960
I guess Akihabara for me is all 
about memories of my dad.

12:19.980 --> 12:21.440
Your dad?

12:21.440 --> 12:22.150
Yeah.

12:22.840 --> 12:24.260
He died, though.

12:24.260 --> 12:27.850
He had lots of interests 
and was like a pure, concentrated otaku.

12:33.780 --> 12:35.770
Dad was a computer otaku.

12:36.230 --> 12:40.560
He used to take me to Akihabara to look 
for magazines and dig for PC parts.

12:40.980 --> 12:44.340
When I think about it now, 
it was like taking an AP course.

12:45.600 --> 12:49.960
Anime, manga, games, figurines, models...

12:50.360 --> 12:52.440
Everything about the city was so vivid.

12:52.440 --> 12:53.960
It was like it sparkled.

12:53.960 --> 12:57.200
Of course, so did 
the people who hung out there.

12:58.960 --> 13:01.710
Otaku would rush off 
the first train to get merch.

12:59.710 --> 13:01.720
<b>Akihabara Store</b>

13:01.720 --> 13:04.840
There were maids, 
people dancing in the street,

13:05.220 --> 13:07.470
Destroy! (Destroy) Destroy! (Destroy)

13:05.220 --> 13:07.470
Kira Kira KILLER

13:05.240 --> 13:07.470
and friends partying at IRL meet-ups.

13:07.470 --> 13:10.720
Otaku clubs strolling down Mansei Bridge, 
following their princesses.

13:11.190 --> 13:14.970
Walking out the Electric Town exit 
to Chuo Street was so exciting!

13:15.540 --> 13:20.000
In Akiba, it felt like 
the whole town was alive.

13:20.000 --> 13:21.020
Alive?

13:21.020 --> 13:21.980
Yeah.

13:22.150 --> 13:24.510
There was a magic spell on the city.

13:24.870 --> 13:26.730
It was the home 
of everything you ever liked.

13:27.940 --> 13:31.020
And I saw that destroyed before my own eyes.

13:33.640 --> 13:36.360
The enemy sealed off Akiba. 
We need to liberate it

13:36.720 --> 13:39.480
and return the world to what it once was.

13:40.400 --> 13:42.760
For that, we need a revolution.

13:42.760 --> 13:45.620
What kind of a world do you imagine?

13:48.880 --> 13:52.890
One where you can like whatever you 
want to like, as much as you want to like it.

13:52.890 --> 13:54.890
Whatever you like...

13:54.890 --> 13:56.390
...as much as you want?

13:56.390 --> 13:58.140
Gobo, gobo-bo.

14:01.590 --> 14:05.240
I want to see that world, too.

14:40.160 --> 14:41.560
Yeah, I know.

14:42.040 --> 14:44.440
I know your souls are somewhere else.

14:44.770 --> 14:48.210
But your deaths were so 
meaningless, so unfair...

14:48.830 --> 14:50.620
I don't ever want to forget.

14:51.630 --> 14:53.590
At least let me mourn.

14:55.400 --> 14:57.890
Even though I know it's none of my business.

14:57.890 --> 14:59.830
Oh, that isn't true at all.

15:02.830 --> 15:06.460
I'm sure they all appreciate it.

15:06.980 --> 15:10.590
They appreciate... and welcome you.

15:13.870 --> 15:14.920
Y-You!

15:14.920 --> 15:17.930
Oh, dear. What an awful smell.

15:17.930 --> 15:21.110
Them, as well as you. You're all pests.

15:21.540 --> 15:26.590
In the midst of such beauty, 
you crawl out and start devouring, gnawing,

15:26.590 --> 15:31.110
like disgusting, bizarre, squirming maggots.

15:31.110 --> 15:33.550
You can't distinguish between 
creation and consumption,

15:33.550 --> 15:38.440
and vomit out garbage words like 
you think you're rewriting the world.

15:38.440 --> 15:42.190
Your mere existence contaminates 
this world like a poison.

15:42.190 --> 15:43.780
That is what otaku are.

15:44.720 --> 15:45.790
Am I wrong?

15:47.540 --> 15:48.900
Totally wron—

15:51.120 --> 15:52.820
How so, then?

15:52.820 --> 15:55.550
Just look at you. You're truly disgusting.

15:56.360 --> 15:58.790
Someday you, too, will end up buried here.

15:59.020 --> 16:02.230
But why don't I give you 
a little room to choose?

16:02.230 --> 16:06.610
The next time we meet, who will achieve 
the world they envisioned?

16:06.610 --> 16:09.810
Will it be you, or will it be me?

16:15.720 --> 16:17.680
I might just enjoy this.

16:28.010 --> 16:30.040
Huh? What are these?

16:30.040 --> 16:32.050
Christmas presents from me.

16:32.050 --> 16:33.130
Really?

16:33.130 --> 16:34.040
Gobo?

16:36.370 --> 16:37.430
Wow!

16:37.430 --> 16:38.760
Gobo gobo gobo!

16:38.760 --> 16:40.300
Clothes for cosplay?

16:40.300 --> 16:42.080
What? These rags?

16:42.080 --> 16:43.310
Yeah, sorry!

16:43.310 --> 16:46.780
When we met, you called 
yourselves magical girls, right?

16:47.310 --> 16:50.150
So I thought I could, at least, 
make you clothes to match.

16:51.290 --> 16:54.400
Yeah, but it's not like we 
can really use magic, anyway.

16:54.400 --> 16:56.310
Why did we even say that?

16:57.620 --> 16:59.050
Now we go our separate ways.

16:59.570 --> 17:00.830
Gobo?

17:00.830 --> 17:02.080
Our separate ways?

17:01.130 --> 17:02.080
Huh?

17:02.080 --> 17:04.460
Tomorrow, I'm starting a revolution.

17:04.460 --> 17:06.630
I can't let you get involved in that.

17:06.630 --> 17:08.590
It's been a year since we met.

17:08.590 --> 17:09.940
It was fun!

17:10.350 --> 17:13.690
I want you to watch from 
a safe distance as we change the world.

17:13.690 --> 17:15.510
Hey, wait a minute.

17:15.510 --> 17:18.640
You're saying that 
because you know it's impossible.

17:19.320 --> 17:22.480
You don't expect to win at all. Do you?

17:23.890 --> 17:27.890
Gobo... gobobo! Gobo gobo gobo-bo!

17:25.120 --> 17:27.890
"But I don't want to! 
I don't want to say goodbye!"

17:27.890 --> 17:30.620
She's right! Did you think 
we'd be okay with thi—?

17:30.620 --> 17:31.440
Hey!

17:32.150 --> 17:34.150
Can I go ahead and try this on?

17:34.150 --> 17:35.020
Sure.

17:35.020 --> 17:36.720
Come on, you, too.

17:44.050 --> 17:47.150
That's against club rules, sir.

17:50.400 --> 17:52.830
Ta-da! Well?

17:54.070 --> 17:55.480
Yeah! It looks great on you!

17:55.480 --> 17:57.760
What? Are you being serious?

17:57.760 --> 17:58.470
Huh?

18:00.760 --> 18:02.340
This isn't cute at all!

18:02.340 --> 18:06.770
Even ignoring the low quality of the
needlework, this is just not...

18:06.770 --> 18:09.100
Gobo-go gobo!

18:07.300 --> 18:09.100
"Design sense: zero!"

18:10.990 --> 18:12.620
What a tough crowd.

18:12.620 --> 18:13.480
Geez!

18:13.480 --> 18:16.780
This is the first Christmas 
present I've ever gotten,

18:16.780 --> 18:20.580
and it's stupid and ugly,
and obviously your fetish!

18:22.140 --> 18:25.220
We really can't... 
count on you for anything.

18:25.740 --> 18:27.280
You're always daydreaming.

18:27.820 --> 18:30.020
You're kind of nice, 
but you're such a chicken.

18:31.120 --> 18:33.760
You're just a stupid otaku.

18:33.760 --> 18:35.140
Gobo...

18:35.880 --> 18:38.090
But you still...

18:43.020 --> 18:44.290
Whoa!

18:45.830 --> 18:48.270
...mean everything to us.

18:45.830 --> 18:48.270
Gobo gobo gobo.

18:59.600 --> 19:03.440
Anarchy-chan? Blue-chan? Pink-chan?

19:04.800 --> 19:07.460
We'll use our magic for you.

19:08.240 --> 19:10.210
We want to fight on your side.

19:10.210 --> 19:13.080
Gobo gobo gobo?

19:10.930 --> 19:13.080
"Will you take us with you?"

19:14.100 --> 19:17.080
To all otaku, and to us,

19:17.080 --> 19:19.350
you're our hero.

19:17.080 --> 19:19.350
Gobo gobo.

19:19.350 --> 19:21.840
Otaku Hero!

19:19.350 --> 19:21.840
Gobobo gobo!

19:43.240 --> 19:44.570
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

20:01.000 --> 20:03.090
Gobo gobo!

20:10.250 --> 20:13.100
Enemy reinforcements on the 
north side of Kuramaebashi Street!

20:13.100 --> 20:16.220
The barricade's too weak! 
What the hell are you doing?!

20:16.820 --> 20:17.990
No way.

20:17.990 --> 20:19.540
<i>Hey! Where are you?</i>

20:19.540 --> 20:21.090
<i>What's taking so long?</i>

20:21.090 --> 20:23.660
Whoa! What's the big deal?

20:23.660 --> 20:25.720
<i>We're totally screwed! We're under attack!</i>

20:25.720 --> 20:28.490
<i>They started a major offensive last night!</i>

20:28.490 --> 20:29.350
What did you say?

20:29.350 --> 20:30.620
A major offensive?

20:30.620 --> 20:32.880
<i>We can't hold them back any longer!</i>

20:34.480 --> 20:37.630
Nick, patch my radio through 
to everyone there.

20:37.630 --> 20:39.380
Got it. Done!

20:41.450 --> 20:42.980
<i>Hey, guys, listen up!</i>

20:43.460 --> 20:44.420
That voice!

20:44.420 --> 20:45.390
Otaku Hero?

20:45.390 --> 20:50.160
<i>You too, SSC. We took Nakano down again!</i>

20:51.150 --> 20:52.900
What? Really?!

20:52.900 --> 20:56.600
<i>It's our second big victory 
since the Nakano Incident.</i>

20:56.600 --> 21:00.150
We aren't going to lose Akiba. 
We'll never hand it over to you!

21:00.470 --> 21:02.000
<i>Keep it up, guys!</i>

21:02.400 --> 21:04.400
<i>We're fighting for our dreams!</i>

21:05.040 --> 21:07.540
<i>Because that's who we are!</i>

21:07.540 --> 21:09.830
<i>Take back our life, our reason to live!</i>

21:10.300 --> 21:11.910
<i>Take back our freedom!</i>

21:12.240 --> 21:16.000
<i>Oppression and persecution 
will never be enough to stop us!</i>

21:16.760 --> 21:18.480
<i>Show them your pride!</i>

21:18.480 --> 21:22.290
<i>What's wrong with liking 
the things we want to like?</i>

21:22.290 --> 21:23.550
We are all

21:24.060 --> 21:26.430
otaku!

21:27.260 --> 21:27.930
<b>O
T
OTAKU
K
U</b>

21:27.930 --> 21:34.180
Yeah!

21:34.180 --> 21:36.090
That did it, Otaku Hero!

21:36.090 --> 21:37.070
<i>Thank God.</i>

21:37.500 --> 21:40.250
<i>Get back quick! We'll hold out somehow!</i>

21:40.250 --> 21:41.980
Okay. You got this, Nick!

21:42.330 --> 21:43.680
Let's hurry back.

21:43.680 --> 21:46.990
Anarchy-chan, do you have 
a spell to get back quickly?

21:47.790 --> 21:48.740
Huh?

21:48.740 --> 21:49.870
What the?

21:49.870 --> 21:50.990
Go-bo?

21:50.990 --> 21:52.490
What the hell?

21:50.990 --> 21:52.490
Gobo bo?

23:25.960 --> 23:28.840
Welcome to a world made just for you.

23:28.840 --> 23:31.290
Trapped in endless cyberbattle.

23:31.290 --> 23:34.160
It's just a little bit 
of your life on the line.

23:34.160 --> 23:36.880
Continue and continue.

23:36.880 --> 23:39.240
Wherever you die, just get back up.
